        <div id="skip-both" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            14. Who Should Skip Both?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Skip both if you are vegan, allergic to milk, or want a whey with no collagen in the protein count. Both are dairy-based blends, both include collagen, and both contain coconut in some form. A plant protein or a single-ingredient whey suits those buyers better; our <a href='/orgain-vs-truvani/'>Orgain vs Truvani</a> comparison covers two clean-label plant options.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip both, too, if cost per gram is your first filter. At $2.46 to $3.00 per 25 g, both cost well above a plain grass-fed whey or a mainstream isolate, and you are paying for the brand, the sweetener choice and the extras. Our <a href='/protein-powder-comparison/'>protein powder comparison</a> sorts every product we have checked by cost per 25 g.
          </p>

          <p>
            People who are lactose sensitive should be cautious with both, since each is built on whey concentrate rather than isolate. Anyone with kidney disease, who is pregnant, or who takes medication should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before adding a daily protein supplement.
          </p>
